{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>מפר אתות בדים.</b> These are those who fabricate from their hearts, and like it: בדיך מתים יחרישו (Job 11:3). And it is more correct that it be from the root בדד, for there are souls that have the power to be alone." "<b>וקוסמים.</b> These are the astrologers, and the meaning is גוזרי', those who say 'so it shall be.' And the בדים are those who say 'so it shall be,' not by way of wisdom." "<b>משיב חכמים.</b> These are seers of the liver and the shoulder, and diviners of the future."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:02.851042753Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}